WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.690
<b>Tenjiku</b>

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.690
<b>Jinko</b>

00:00:02.040 --> 00:00:03.920
Jinko won.

00:00:06.030 --> 00:00:09.990
Damn, I genuinely enjoyed that game.

00:00:09.990 --> 00:00:13.450
I can't believe they beat 
an Osaka quarterfinalist.

00:00:13.450 --> 00:00:17.260
Jinko's gotten stronger.

00:00:19.420 --> 00:00:21.580
Are we not going to say hello to them?

00:00:22.490 --> 00:00:25.580
That was the first and last time
we'll cheer for them.

00:00:26.250 --> 00:00:29.640
There's no need to go say hello
to formidable foes.

00:00:32.890 --> 00:00:34.010
Bow!

00:00:34.010 --> 00:00:36.490
Good game!

00:02:18.810 --> 00:02:21.660
Jinko! We did it!

00:02:21.660 --> 00:02:23.980
What are you crying for, Ume-chan?

00:02:21.660 --> 00:02:26.720
<b>#20
 Aren't You Happy?</b>

00:02:23.980 --> 00:02:27.880
Because... Because how long 
has it been since our last win?

00:02:27.880 --> 00:02:30.460
Ume-chan-san, congratulations!

00:02:30.460 --> 00:02:32.250
That was amazing!

00:02:48.140 --> 00:02:51.810
What's the deal with you guys? 
You're freakin' strong.

00:02:52.190 --> 00:02:55.360
Who called 'em "nobodies"?

00:02:55.360 --> 00:02:57.340
Ukyo, was it you?

00:02:57.340 --> 00:02:58.940
N-No, it was <i>you</i>!

00:02:59.260 --> 00:03:02.150
Your tackles owned!

00:03:02.150 --> 00:03:05.700
If you'd tackled me like that, 
you'd've knocked out my front teeth!

00:03:05.700 --> 00:03:06.660
Th-Thanks.

00:03:07.950 --> 00:03:10.130
You should've told us you were strong.

00:03:10.130 --> 00:03:12.780
Seriously, that was irritatin'.

00:03:12.780 --> 00:03:15.460
Thanks, man.

00:03:17.210 --> 00:03:19.920
Why aren't you saying anythin'?

00:03:20.680 --> 00:03:22.330
W-Well, actually...

00:03:23.230 --> 00:03:27.630
Th-This is the first time we've won a game.

00:03:28.840 --> 00:03:30.900
We don't know how to celebrate.

00:03:32.990 --> 00:03:35.480
Pull the other one!

00:03:37.500 --> 00:03:38.980
Komori-san...

00:03:39.870 --> 00:03:41.360
Thank you.

00:03:41.360 --> 00:03:43.710
We learned a lot from you.

00:03:45.550 --> 00:03:46.990
No, thank you.

00:03:46.990 --> 00:03:50.760
It was an honor to play against 
one of Osaka's quarterfinalists.

00:03:54.260 --> 00:03:57.350
Pack up your stuff, boys! We're leavin'!

00:03:57.350 --> 00:03:59.190
Yes, sir.

00:04:04.610 --> 00:04:06.950
Sunao-san, nice work out there.

00:04:06.950 --> 00:04:08.910
Were you okay?

00:04:08.910 --> 00:04:12.120
Hey, Toru. I'm fine now.

00:04:12.120 --> 00:04:17.690
Sorry I missed that kick. I was useless.

00:04:17.920 --> 00:04:20.920
Hey, the insolent first-year's apologizin'.

00:04:20.920 --> 00:04:22.240
He never does that!

00:04:22.240 --> 00:04:26.320
Shut your trap!
What Sunao-san said made me think.

00:04:28.480 --> 00:04:30.200
I'll work harder.

00:04:30.200 --> 00:04:34.180
I promise I'll take you guys to Hanazono.

00:04:34.960 --> 00:04:37.450
I can't believe how insolent this punk is!

00:04:37.450 --> 00:04:38.840
Get him!

00:04:41.840 --> 00:04:43.000
Renpei...

00:04:43.570 --> 00:04:45.090
Hey. Hey, you.

00:04:45.480 --> 00:04:48.390
Nice game. You're Osaka Sunao-kun, right?

00:04:48.390 --> 00:04:49.230
Yes.

00:04:49.230 --> 00:04:52.850
I'm Iwakura of Kyoto Sankei University.

00:04:52.850 --> 00:04:55.050
I watched your game.

00:04:55.050 --> 00:04:59.870
It's too bad how it turned out, 
but your movements were good.

00:04:59.870 --> 00:05:02.210
I'm not talking about your technique...

00:05:02.210 --> 00:05:05.110
Um, I guess you could say you 
showed a different kind of spirit.

00:05:05.580 --> 00:05:08.360
I've already talked to Sakura-kun,

00:05:08.360 --> 00:05:11.870
but honestly, I think you have more potential.

00:05:15.680 --> 00:05:17.620
This is for you, Renpei.

00:05:21.170 --> 00:05:25.280
Renpei, you belong on the national team!

00:05:26.130 --> 00:05:27.860
What? Why?

00:05:27.860 --> 00:05:31.390
'Cause your family name's Sakura.

00:05:31.390 --> 00:05:34.610
The national team has <i>sakura</i> 
cherry blossoms on their chests.

00:05:34.610 --> 00:05:38.120
No one's better suited to 
wearin' that jersey than you.

00:05:41.540 --> 00:05:43.520
Yeah, you're right.

00:05:43.520 --> 00:05:46.440
Since my name's Sakura, 
I'd look great in this jersey.

00:05:46.440 --> 00:05:47.700
I'll wear it someday.

00:05:47.700 --> 00:05:51.050
Yeah, I'm sure you will.

00:05:51.050 --> 00:05:54.080
And when you do, I'll be first 
in line to get your autograph.

00:06:01.000 --> 00:06:04.300
Iwakura 
Takuo

00:06:01.410 --> 00:06:04.300
If you haven't decided on 
a school yet, come to ours.

00:06:04.300 --> 00:06:05.890
We'd be glad to have you.

00:06:06.830 --> 00:06:08.600
Thank you.

00:06:09.610 --> 00:06:11.970
Sunao got a business card!

00:06:11.970 --> 00:06:13.450
Where's he from?

00:06:13.450 --> 00:06:14.910
What? Kyoto Sankei?

00:06:14.910 --> 00:06:15.930
I hear that place is crazy.

00:06:16.320 --> 00:06:19.190
Hey, guys! Let's go!

00:06:19.190 --> 00:06:21.260
Let's go, Suna-chan.

00:06:21.260 --> 00:06:22.700
Yeah, sure.

00:06:29.910 --> 00:06:33.160
Iwakura 
Takuo

00:06:30.920 --> 00:06:33.160
<i>Potential, huh?</i>

00:06:33.160 --> 00:06:36.230
<i>I ain't nowhere near national level.</i>

00:06:41.420 --> 00:06:45.000
Renpei, you've got leaves in your hair.

00:06:45.330 --> 00:06:50.300
Renpei, let's play foosball
 at the souvenir shop again later.

00:06:50.300 --> 00:06:52.660
You've never beaten me, have you?

00:06:52.660 --> 00:06:55.280
I've got a feeling 
I'll trounce you this year.

00:07:01.360 --> 00:07:03.660
Next time, let's meet at Hanazono!

00:07:10.150 --> 00:07:12.660
<b>Ikuta Inn</b>

00:07:12.130 --> 00:07:14.900
And then Jinko won the game!

00:07:14.900 --> 00:07:16.030
It was amazing!

00:07:16.030 --> 00:07:19.180
They even made these really difficult kicks!

00:07:16.030 --> 00:07:22.420
<b>Reception</b>

00:07:19.180 --> 00:07:21.880
Oh, and I was so surprised when 
they lifted a guy into the air!

00:07:21.880 --> 00:07:23.140
And their opponents—

00:07:23.140 --> 00:07:23.710
Miki.

00:07:24.260 --> 00:07:26.710
Have you ever watched a rugby game before?

00:07:26.710 --> 00:07:28.370
No, never.

00:07:28.370 --> 00:07:31.520
Then, you don't know what 
an amazing play looks like.

00:07:32.120 --> 00:07:34.510
W-Well, maybe not, but...

00:07:34.510 --> 00:07:38.120
There's no way a team as slovenly 
as Jinko could produce the goods.

00:07:38.120 --> 00:07:40.230
Rugby's not that easy.

00:07:40.230 --> 00:07:43.130
Their opponents must've been weak, too.

00:07:43.130 --> 00:07:47.360
B-But they said they were
 quarterfinalists in Osaka...

00:07:47.760 --> 00:07:49.040
Osaka?

00:07:50.050 --> 00:07:53.700
Must've gone easy on them 
since it was a practice game.

00:07:53.700 --> 00:07:55.260
Really?

00:07:55.260 --> 00:07:58.100
It didn't look like either side
was taking it easy to me...

00:07:58.100 --> 00:08:00.370
It's almost time to serve dinner.

00:08:00.370 --> 00:08:01.120
Let's go.

00:08:03.680 --> 00:08:07.590
<i>They looked serious to me...</i>

00:08:09.340 --> 00:08:10.590
Excuse me!

00:08:10.590 --> 00:08:12.650
Dinner is—

00:08:16.650 --> 00:08:17.500
What?

00:08:19.280 --> 00:08:21.270
U-Um...

00:08:21.270 --> 00:08:24.770
What's going on here? Did they get creamed?

00:08:24.770 --> 00:08:27.400
No, they won. They <i>definitely</i> won.

00:08:40.410 --> 00:08:42.700
E-Enjoy your meal.

00:09:00.280 --> 00:09:02.980
Congratulations. Well done.

00:09:03.780 --> 00:09:05.510
It was a good game.

00:09:06.480 --> 00:09:09.420
It's been three months since I joined Jinko.

00:09:10.490 --> 00:09:14.240
I'm sorry I couldn't lead you
 to victory until now.

00:09:16.210 --> 00:09:19.020
Captain, do you have 
anything you want to say?

00:09:25.960 --> 00:09:29.310
Well, uh...

00:09:30.870 --> 00:09:33.070
Everyone worked hard.

00:09:33.870 --> 00:09:38.150
Both the guys fighting on the field 
and the guys cheering from the sidelines.

00:09:38.720 --> 00:09:42.800
We prepared really hard, and...

00:09:44.110 --> 00:09:45.350
Captain.

00:09:46.170 --> 00:09:51.860
One of the unspoken rules of rugby is 
not to celebrate your victories too much.

00:09:52.440 --> 00:09:55.340
You must show consideration 
for the losing team.

00:09:57.380 --> 00:10:02.700
They say you shouldn't celebrate 
excessively, even when you score a try.

00:10:03.080 --> 00:10:04.790
Because you didn't do it alone.

00:10:04.790 --> 00:10:07.260
The entire team passed 
the ball along the line,

00:10:07.260 --> 00:10:11.840
and you just happened 
to be waiting at the end.

00:10:13.230 --> 00:10:16.400
But there are only Jinko players in this room.

00:10:18.150 --> 00:10:20.670
Aren't you happy?

00:10:27.740 --> 00:10:30.090
I'm really happy!

00:10:31.630 --> 00:10:34.860
Then show it, you idiots.

00:10:34.860 --> 00:10:37.360
Yeah!

00:10:37.360 --> 00:10:38.860
Dinner!

00:10:38.860 --> 00:10:41.870
We really beat a team
that made the Osaka quarters!

00:10:41.870 --> 00:10:44.030
Kifune, you were a star out there.

00:10:44.030 --> 00:10:46.620
You'd better show me your bag of tricks later!

00:10:47.430 --> 00:10:49.870
Today's a special occasion.

00:10:49.870 --> 00:10:51.800
Captain, want a drink?

00:10:51.800 --> 00:10:53.460
Yes, sir. What?

00:10:53.460 --> 00:10:56.180
You can't do that!
What are you talking about?

00:11:00.160 --> 00:11:02.590
See? I told you. They won.

00:11:02.590 --> 00:11:06.060
Yeah. What a bunch of weirdos.

00:11:06.720 --> 00:11:09.310
Has Jinko always been like that?

00:11:12.200 --> 00:11:15.310
Gion-kun, c-congratulations on your first try.

00:11:16.680 --> 00:11:18.440
You were amazing, Gion.

00:11:21.450 --> 00:11:25.450
<b>I finally played 
in a game today.</b>

00:11:21.450 --> 00:11:25.450
Yeah, but I wish I could've 
sprinted down-field

00:11:25.450 --> 00:11:27.700
and scored a try like the truant delinquent.

00:11:27.700 --> 00:11:31.100
Did you say something, you little turd?

00:11:33.480 --> 00:11:34.080
<b>I finally played 
in a game today.</b>

00:11:34.130 --> 00:11:36.590
<b>Apparently, one
 of my classmates...</b>

00:11:36.630 --> 00:11:40.590
<b>...scored his first try today. 
Even though we were in the 
middle of the game, 
he cried right then and there.</b>

00:11:40.630 --> 00:11:41.720
<b>It was only a practice 
game, too. Weird, right?</b>

00:11:48.720 --> 00:11:51.230
<b>Tacchan</b>

00:11:48.720 --> 00:11:51.230
<b>Sounds like an 
funny guy (lol).
 What's he like?</b>

00:11:53.840 --> 00:11:55.570
Hey, Gion-kun.

00:11:55.570 --> 00:11:56.060
Huh?

00:11:56.060 --> 00:11:57.240
Look this way.

00:11:59.870 --> 00:12:02.400
<i>"He looks like this."</i>

00:12:04.410 --> 00:12:07.910
<b>Ikuta Inn</b>

00:12:05.150 --> 00:12:06.850
I caught him looking stupid.

00:12:07.910 --> 00:12:10.930
<b>Renpei!</b>

00:12:07.910 --> 00:12:10.930
<b>One more time! 
Let's play one more time!</b>

00:12:08.910 --> 00:12:10.930
<b>No way</b>

00:12:10.930 --> 00:12:13.920
<b>I told you, 
that's my team</b>

00:12:10.930 --> 00:12:13.920
<b>Whomp</b>

00:12:15.430 --> 00:12:17.430
I'm exhausted.

00:12:17.950 --> 00:12:20.900
Ume-chan-san, you really are amazing.

00:12:20.900 --> 00:12:22.790
What? How?

00:12:22.790 --> 00:12:26.600
From dawn till dusk, 
all you do is work for the team.

00:12:26.600 --> 00:12:30.700
Well, yeah. It's hard work, 
but I'm the team's only manager.

00:12:30.700 --> 00:12:32.890
I can't exactly quit.

00:12:32.890 --> 00:12:36.180
Hey, did you find anyone 
on our team handsome?

00:12:36.180 --> 00:12:39.700
What? They're all handsome.

00:12:39.700 --> 00:12:43.310
And there it is! You know that's not true.

00:12:43.310 --> 00:12:45.530
But I feel like they'd all be popular.

00:12:45.890 --> 00:12:49.580
That was my first time seeing rugby players,
and they looked so cool out there.

00:12:49.580 --> 00:12:50.790
I don't know about that.

00:12:51.110 --> 00:12:55.790
At school, people treat them 
like they're loud and annoying.

00:12:55.790 --> 00:12:59.420
Ume-chan-san, are you dating anyone?

00:13:00.100 --> 00:13:03.520
No way! Not at all!

00:13:03.520 --> 00:13:05.680
I can see your stomach.

00:13:06.840 --> 00:13:08.990
I bet the captain's popular.

00:13:09.760 --> 00:13:12.110
His looks send people running the other way.

00:13:12.110 --> 00:13:16.000
Come to think of it, in the rugby world,

00:13:16.000 --> 00:13:20.590
they say you should marry someone
who plays in a position with a small number.

00:13:20.590 --> 00:13:21.570
What? Why?

00:13:21.570 --> 00:13:27.040
The backs are skinny and fast. 
A lot of them are all show.

00:13:26.470 --> 00:13:29.830
<b>Handsome

00:13:26.470 --> 00:13:29.830
<b>Can carry 
heavy things 

00:13:27.040 --> 00:13:29.820
Forwards seem like
they're all brawn and no brain,

00:13:30.040 --> 00:13:31.930
but a lot of them are nice.

00:13:31.930 --> 00:13:33.200
I see.

00:13:33.200 --> 00:13:36.060
On our team, that would be #2, Hachi-san.

00:13:36.060 --> 00:13:38.430
He's a magnanimous chubster!

00:13:36.310 --> 00:13:40.170
I'll carry your things

00:13:38.900 --> 00:13:40.170
He does seem nice.

00:13:40.170 --> 00:13:45.730
#3, Hirota-san, is a little removed 
from what make forwards attractive.

00:13:44.940 --> 00:13:50.680
Feed me

00:13:46.610 --> 00:13:50.680
But it does feel good to watch
 someone who eats a lot.

00:13:50.680 --> 00:13:54.680
At around #9 or #10 and above,
you get guys a little full of themselves.

00:13:54.680 --> 00:13:56.970
On our team, that's Oharano.

00:13:56.970 --> 00:13:59.120
He's handsome and smart, though.

00:13:59.120 --> 00:14:01.690
Oh, he's like a prince.

00:13:59.330 --> 00:14:01.690
Can't you be smarter?

00:14:01.690 --> 00:14:06.320
Once you get to the wings,
their showiness increases significantly.

00:14:05.960 --> 00:14:20.080
Shut up and follow me

00:14:06.320 --> 00:14:11.110
Ebumi's pretty popular even 
though he's as rough as they come.

00:14:11.110 --> 00:14:13.560
Even newbies to the sport find it cool

00:14:13.560 --> 00:14:15.770
when a guy sprints down 
the field to score a try.

00:14:15.770 --> 00:14:20.610
Our #15s are either average, 
or just too timid.

00:14:17.480 --> 00:14:18.100
Kibi

00:14:18.690 --> 00:14:19.350
Kifune

00:14:20.610 --> 00:14:22.510
The positions tend to be that way,

00:14:22.510 --> 00:14:25.190
so it's better to marry positions 
with smaller numbers.

00:14:25.190 --> 00:14:26.590
I see.

00:14:26.590 --> 00:14:29.760
Who did you like the most, Miki-chan?

00:14:31.830 --> 00:14:35.630
I think Hirota-san is more
 my type of all of them.

00:14:34.180 --> 00:14:37.850
<b>Meanwhile,
 Hirota...</b>

00:14:35.630 --> 00:14:36.410
What?

00:14:38.860 --> 00:14:40.650
Oh, really?

00:14:43.130 --> 00:14:48.860
I can't believe we're really going drinking.

00:14:49.880 --> 00:14:51.660
Of course we are.

00:14:52.190 --> 00:14:55.290
I never use niceties for the sake of it.

00:15:02.350 --> 00:15:03.990
Thank you.

00:15:04.650 --> 00:15:05.920
For what?

00:15:07.440 --> 00:15:10.690
Oh, don't worry about the reservation.

00:15:10.690 --> 00:15:12.450
They know me there.

00:15:12.450 --> 00:15:14.640
That's not what I meant.

00:15:16.120 --> 00:15:18.390
We'll be busy starting tomorrow.

00:15:18.390 --> 00:15:20.990
We should kick back and relax while we can.

00:15:23.200 --> 00:15:26.830
I've actually also invited 
someone else to come drink with us.

00:15:29.710 --> 00:15:32.750
Sorry. Did you wait long, Futami-san?

00:15:32.750 --> 00:15:35.130
Oh, no. I just got here.

00:15:35.130 --> 00:15:36.370
Thanks for earlier.

00:15:36.370 --> 00:15:38.000
Hello, Teach.

00:15:40.050 --> 00:15:40.750
All right, then.

00:15:40.750 --> 00:15:42.580
Cheers!

00:15:48.770 --> 00:15:49.840
So good.

00:15:49.840 --> 00:15:53.470
Futami-san, did you play rugby?

00:15:53.470 --> 00:15:56.060
Yes, sir. I used to play wing.

00:15:56.060 --> 00:15:57.580
I see.

00:15:57.580 --> 00:16:00.580
It's been four years 
since I started coaching.

00:16:01.140 --> 00:16:04.190
I'm 32 this year.

00:16:04.190 --> 00:16:06.160
What? We're the same age?

00:16:06.160 --> 00:16:09.190
You, too? What a coincidence.

00:16:09.190 --> 00:16:11.430
You look so young...

00:16:11.430 --> 00:16:14.570
Not at all. I'm an old man.

00:16:18.120 --> 00:16:18.990
As a young coach,

00:16:18.990 --> 00:16:21.960
it must be hard to establish the right 
distance between yourself and your players.

00:16:22.960 --> 00:16:26.840
Here are your pickles, 
edamame, and julienned yams.

00:16:28.750 --> 00:16:30.760
One draft beer, please.

00:16:31.770 --> 00:16:34.320
I'm actually worried about that right now.

00:16:34.800 --> 00:16:39.260
You didn't say much to the Tenjiku boys.

00:16:39.850 --> 00:16:41.090
Is that your coaching philosophy?

00:16:41.090 --> 00:16:42.390
Here's your beer.

00:16:42.390 --> 00:16:43.140
Thanks.

00:16:46.480 --> 00:16:48.400
At first, I did.

00:16:48.820 --> 00:16:51.630
How should I put it? Oh, you know...

00:16:51.630 --> 00:16:54.900
I was an overly enthusiastic new teacher.

00:16:55.160 --> 00:16:57.800
We promised we'd get stronger together.

00:16:58.410 --> 00:17:01.120
I helped all of them train individually, too.

00:17:02.880 --> 00:17:06.120
I'd visit them at home in the evening
to listen to their concerns.

00:17:07.080 --> 00:17:09.170
I wanted to be like that.

00:17:10.260 --> 00:17:11.380
I was desperate.

00:17:12.250 --> 00:17:17.900
But once they get stronger, 
they start to change.

00:17:19.560 --> 00:17:22.850
They started to act like it was 
only natural that they'd win.

00:17:23.580 --> 00:17:27.140
They started wanting to practice difficult 
techniques rather than fundamentals.

00:17:27.610 --> 00:17:30.070
I started being talked over, too.

00:17:31.100 --> 00:17:34.320
They stopped doing what I told them to do, 
no matter how many times I showed them.

00:17:34.820 --> 00:17:41.580
But since the team had a lot of guys who 
had a feel for the game, they kept winning.

00:17:42.280 --> 00:17:47.330
So I tried leaving it all
up to them this time.

00:17:47.730 --> 00:17:49.170
I wanted to see how 
much they could handle.

00:17:51.400 --> 00:17:52.590
The truth is...

00:17:56.970 --> 00:18:00.160
I wanted to see them lose.

00:18:01.620 --> 00:18:04.580
I know it's an awful thing to do.

00:18:04.580 --> 00:18:07.020
I watched my boys play
and prayed that they'd lose.

00:18:07.840 --> 00:18:12.770
Every one of them has the skills, 
but they lack the right emotions.

00:18:13.610 --> 00:18:15.920
They lack the desire to pass the ball along.

00:18:15.920 --> 00:18:17.530
The determination not to lose.

00:18:18.450 --> 00:18:21.030
Skill comes later.

00:18:21.410 --> 00:18:24.430
After watching Jinko play, that's how I felt.

00:18:27.310 --> 00:18:28.660
You're right.

00:18:29.550 --> 00:18:34.170
If it all came down to individual skill,
we wouldn't have stood a chance.

00:18:34.990 --> 00:18:37.220
What a nice shtory.

00:18:37.220 --> 00:18:41.480
I actually asked Keijo to play us first.

00:18:42.820 --> 00:18:45.290
Could I get some sake?

00:18:42.820 --> 00:18:46.080
Haijima-san and I have a mutual friend.

00:18:46.080 --> 00:18:47.300
Haijima-shan?

00:18:47.300 --> 00:18:49.690
Uh, yeah. Haijima-san.

00:18:50.250 --> 00:18:51.270
One beer!

00:18:51.270 --> 00:18:53.000
Two beers, please.

00:18:53.000 --> 00:18:55.940
Simply because Keijo is a powerhouse,

00:18:55.940 --> 00:18:58.590
and I heard they play dirty.

00:18:59.940 --> 00:19:01.680
You thought they'd beat you.

00:19:01.680 --> 00:19:02.200
Yeah.

00:19:02.700 --> 00:19:06.750
But Haijima-san told me 
there was a better school.

00:19:06.750 --> 00:19:08.030
Here.

00:19:08.780 --> 00:19:10.370
Uh, thank you.

00:19:10.370 --> 00:19:13.230
But you have to believe me.

00:19:13.680 --> 00:19:15.440
We underestimated you at first,

00:19:15.440 --> 00:19:18.260
but they were doing their best
in the second half.

00:19:18.800 --> 00:19:23.510
Even after we got back, they were 
talking about the game over dinner,

00:19:23.830 --> 00:19:25.620
and when they were in the bath.

00:19:27.540 --> 00:19:30.870
"That wasn't good." "This was amazing."

00:19:30.870 --> 00:19:33.230
They were arguing about it the whole time.

00:19:33.780 --> 00:19:35.770
How cute.

00:19:36.540 --> 00:19:37.780
It <i>is </i>cute!

00:19:37.780 --> 00:19:41.370
Lately, they'd been fighting all 
the time and acting like adults.

00:19:41.370 --> 00:19:42.770
They were insolent.

00:19:43.740 --> 00:19:45.910
They finally reverted to being kids again.

00:19:45.910 --> 00:19:48.220
One beer, pleash!

00:19:48.220 --> 00:19:51.790
Futami-san, let me say one thing.

00:19:53.010 --> 00:19:55.980
You can't descend to your players' level

00:19:55.980 --> 00:20:00.320
and be surprised by what you 
learned from today's game.

00:20:00.920 --> 00:20:06.430
A coach must always be the one
surprising his players.

00:20:06.870 --> 00:20:09.610
It's fine to be an older brother figure

00:20:09.610 --> 00:20:13.350
who listens to their concerns and 
who they can speak openly with.

00:20:13.770 --> 00:20:18.820
But more than that,
children want something to surprise them.

00:20:20.130 --> 00:20:22.070
You should put on airs.

00:20:23.100 --> 00:20:26.390
"If I keep following this guy, 
then something might happen."

00:20:27.080 --> 00:20:32.400
You'd be surprised to know that they'll all 
follow you based on that thought alone.

00:20:34.140 --> 00:20:36.220
Good luck to us both.

00:20:41.810 --> 00:20:44.140
Hey, Minakami-shan!

00:20:44.140 --> 00:20:45.390
It's Futami...

00:20:45.390 --> 00:20:48.520
Hey, Komo-san!

00:20:48.520 --> 00:20:49.350
Shut up!

00:20:49.670 --> 00:20:51.350
So this is where you've been?

00:20:51.350 --> 00:20:54.500
I have two mossh ballsh at home.

00:20:54.500 --> 00:20:55.850
T-Two?

00:20:56.920 --> 00:20:59.370
You should've told me the name of the store.

00:20:59.370 --> 00:21:01.950
They have nameshhh.

00:21:01.950 --> 00:21:03.490
Th-The moss balls?

00:21:04.510 --> 00:21:05.490
Mokichi.

00:21:06.640 --> 00:21:07.760
Yoshida-san.

00:21:07.760 --> 00:21:09.020
Get me a beer!

00:21:09.020 --> 00:21:10.070
Shut up!

00:21:10.070 --> 00:21:12.000
And six orders of horse sashimi!

00:21:12.000 --> 00:21:13.940
And Moshuki.

00:21:15.390 --> 00:21:17.000
They're both dudes?

00:21:17.380 --> 00:21:20.740
This is Tenjiku High's coach, Futami-san.

00:21:20.740 --> 00:21:24.170
Oh, hello. I'm Todo-dai Sagami's coach, Kita.

00:21:24.170 --> 00:21:25.560
Nice to meet you.

00:21:25.560 --> 00:21:26.850
Here's your beer.

00:21:26.850 --> 00:21:28.560
Thank you.

00:21:28.560 --> 00:21:30.010
I'd like shome konjac noodleshhh.

00:21:31.150 --> 00:21:32.170
Why?

00:21:32.170 --> 00:21:33.770
Let's do a toast.

00:21:33.770 --> 00:21:35.890
Cheers!

00:21:39.090 --> 00:21:41.770
You're an all right guy, Yoshida-shan.

00:21:41.770 --> 00:21:43.770
I told you, I'm Futami.

00:21:43.770 --> 00:21:45.150
You're Yoshida!

00:21:45.570 --> 00:21:46.710
No, it'shhh you.

00:21:46.710 --> 00:21:49.030
Excuse me, could we get 
some water for this guy?

00:21:49.610 --> 00:21:51.910
Yoshida-sensei, I'm cutting you off.

00:21:51.910 --> 00:21:54.490
What? Why?

00:21:54.490 --> 00:21:56.620
We have to be up early tomorrow.

00:21:56.620 --> 00:21:57.170
What?

00:21:57.170 --> 00:22:00.470
Komo-san, who are you playing tomorrow?

00:22:00.470 --> 00:22:01.990
Maybe I'll come watch.

00:22:01.990 --> 00:22:02.990
Maybe I'll come watch.

00:22:02.990 --> 00:22:05.430
Tomorrow, we're playing Oita's Saeki Maejo.

00:22:05.430 --> 00:22:06.540
Could I have thish one, pleash?

00:22:06.540 --> 00:22:08.300
Hey, Yoshida! I told you to stop drinking!

00:22:08.300 --> 00:22:10.040
You can't do that, Yoshida-shan!

00:22:10.040 --> 00:22:11.940
You're Yoshida!

00:22:11.940 --> 00:22:13.530
You are!

00:23:44.940 --> 00:23:49.940
<b>Next Time "Good Luck Charm"</b>

00:23:46.180 --> 00:23:48.470
Next time: "Good Luck Charm."
